","/arc-plc/arkansas/clark-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025. On the middle of the county&rsquo;s grids, August to September came in under 90% of normal in 36 of those years, and October to November did the same. In 2025 the middle got 166% of normal in April to May but just 45% in November to December. Grid 17246 had its driest year in 2005 at 61%.</p>"}
